 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Boundary Checking:** Performed at the start of the kernel and after each step. If the fragment is out of bounds initially, it returns early (implicitly by not writing or writing 0 if initialized, though the source implies early exit logic in the loop condition) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** The output format is `R8`, which limits the dynamic range of the precomputed light intensities. High dynamic range scenes may suffer from banding or loss of detail in shadows [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If `light_sample_count` is 0, `step_size` becomes undefined (division by zero). The source specifies a range of $[0, 128]$, implying 0 might be handled as a special case or clamped [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Threshold Logic:** The condition `density < density_threshold` treats low-density voxels as transparent unless god rays conditions are met. This can create artifacts if the threshold is set too high, causing large volumes to appear completely black.
+*   **Boundary Conditions:** Boundary checking is performed at the start of the kernel and after each step. If the fragment is out of bounds initially, it returns early (implicitly by not writing or writing 0 if initialized, though the source implies early exit logic) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** The use of `R8` format for the output texture may limit precision for light intensity values [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Thresholding:** The `density_threshold` parameter is critical for filtering noise; densities below this value are treated as transparent unless god rays conditions are met [S1, unofficial].
